  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>St Thomas University Canada is a liberal art and education specialist in Fredericton, New Brunswick. The establishment mainly offers undergraduate courses in various subject areas. Among these are.30 programs in fields including social sciences and humanities.</p><p>The university is known for its small intake of students to provide opportunities and support for all attendees. With just under 2,000 students, an intimate community feel exists on campus at St Thomas. Students can also integrate into the wider community in nearby Fredericton.</p><p>At St Thomas, students can find all the necessary resources on campus. Furthermore, James Dunn Hall is a place for students to socialise with an on-campus cafe, bars and a restaurant.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>St Thomas provides a comfortable and sociable environment for students on campus. As a result, lower-year students can find accommodation options in three separate houses at the university. Harrington Hall, Vanier Hall and Holy Cross House have single, double and private suite options. All accommodation has modern resources, such as internet, study areas, TV lounges, laundry facilities and snack machines.</p><p>However, upper-year students are still part of the university's community and are housed in the off-campus Windsor Street Residences. These are shared student houses run by the university to provide a communal living space.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>St Thomas also has various sports resources, such as a fitness centre and an all-weather pitch.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>The university has a library with computer labs, study areas and material for all undergraduate and postgraduate courses.</p>",
